<title>USA: Argentina sets $2 bln 20-yr global bond-JP Morgan.</title>
<headline>Argentina sets $2 bln 20-yr global bond-JP Morgan.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentina is issuing a $2 billion, 20-year global bond priced at 99.416 to yield 11.45 percent, co-lead manager J.P. Morgan said.</p>
<p>The coupon for the issue is 11.375 percent, to yield 462.5 basis points over comparable U.S. Treasuries.</p>
<p>The issue was 3.5 times oversubscribed, J.P. Morgan said.</p>
<p>The issue is rated B-1 by Moody's Investors Service and BB-minus by Standard &amp; Poor's Corp.</p>
<p>Merrill Lynch is the other co-lead manager.</p>
<p>(( -- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660 ))</p>
